# cottage_interior_offset.cam — a NES/SNES isometric room: the floor of a cube with the
# two near walls cut away (Phase 29 slice 2; DECISIONS.md → "Phase 29 slice 2…").
#
# Two free edges the tool may run off, two CLOSED walls meeting at an INTERIOR
# 90 DEGREE CORNER at (110, 90). Every other wall in this corpus is an arc or a
# straight run of blank; this is the first corner where two walls meet, and it
# is the place no tool of nonzero radius reaches — so what the pattern leaves
# there is the question the fixture exists to ask.
#
# The walls are declared as what they are — standing material — and NOTHING
# says which of the floor's edges are closed. That is derived: a boss standing
# beyond an edge, above this floor, closes it.
units mm
feed 800
plunge 300
rapid_z 5
clearance_z 25
spindle 3000
stock Box(w=120, l=100, h=20, x=0, y=0, z=0)
tool T5 Endmill(dia=10.0)

feature Floor Face(z=-6
    loop
        10 10
        110 10
        110 90
        10 90
)
feature WallE ProfileBoss(extent=6
    110 90
    120 90
    120 10
    110 10
)
feature WallN ProfileBoss(extent=6
    10 100
    120 100
    120 90
    10 90
)
run End(tool=T5, surface=Floor, stepover=5.0, pattern=offset)
